-- Plan 56 criterion 3: a borrowed capture is **rustc's** error, at the
-- generated closure, reported against the line the author wrote.
--
-- `prefix` takes two arguments and is given one, so plan 56 lowers it to
-- `|__rdx_1| prefix(s.as_str(), __rdx_1)` — a closure borrowing `s`, which
-- the function then hands back. Redox has no borrow checker and must never
-- grow one (AGENTS.md), so §1.3's claim is that rustc judges the capture, and
-- this fixture is the claim being tested rather than reasoned about.
--
-- rustc's own advice here is *"use the `move` keyword"*, which plan 56 §5
-- criterion 6 deliberately declines: `move` would turn this borrow error into
-- a move error, which is a worse message about the same mistake, and it would
-- also make the partial application's closure differ in shape from an
-- operator section's. §11.2 is the finding.

prefix : &str -> &str -> String
prefix a b = "#{a}#{b}"

make_prefixer : Box<dyn Fn(&str) -> String>
make_prefixer = Box::new (prefix (.as_str s))
  where
    s = String::from "hi "

main : ()
main =
  shout = make_prefixer ()
  println! \-> "#{(shout "there")}"
  ()
